  "answer": "These correct TEXTUNDO.json's single readings. Cmd+Z in an edit takes one step of typing, not all of it. aa, a pause over 1 s, bb: Cmd+Z leaves aa with the edit open, Cmd+Shift+Z brings bb back, and leaving the edit counts 2 steps. 2 of 2, and a run of 4 single keys also goes back 1 key at a time. The Undo button during an edit takes the last typing only and leaves the edit: the text bar goes and the block is no longer selected. An earlier edit stays: first plus cc gives first, 2 of 2, and the same with a quick earlier edit, 2 of 2. One edit alone: empty, the edit left, the block stays, 2 of 2. Redo lights up.",
  "ours": "Cmd+Z takes all the typing: aabb to empty, and the count after Cmd+Shift+Z is 1. The Undo button takes the earlier edit too, firstcc to empty, and the edit stays open. One edit alone: empty, the block not editable, but the text bar still shows. Read in Chrome. scripts/text-check.mjs:130 pins the old read: it expects back to the start and the edit open.",
  "differs": [
    "Cmd+Z in an edit: oracle takes one step, ours all the typing. After it the oracle counts each step, ours 1.",
